OpenLiteSpeed 1.9.3 — do not crash when statDir is unset and /dev/shm is absent.

configServerBasics(): with no `statDir` directive the server probes /dev/shm;
when that does not exist (macOS, minimal containers) pValue stays NULL and the
strcmp() a few lines later dereferences it. The server dies with SIGSEGV before
writing its first log line — even `openlitespeed -t` exits 139. Measured on
macOS 26 / arm64, 4 Oct 2026. Fix: fall back to the runtime directory, which is
what sStatDir already defaults to. Upstreamable as-is.

diff --git a/src/main/httpserver.cpp b/src/main/httpserver.cpp
index 882dcec..ead2295 100644
--- a/src/main/httpserver.cpp
+++ b/src/main/httpserver.cpp
@@ -4106,6 +4106,11 @@ int HttpServerImpl::configServerBasics(int reconfig, const XmlNode *pRoot)
             {
                 pValue = "/dev/shm/ols/status";
             }
+            /* No /dev/shm (macOS, some containers): pValue stayed NULL and the
+             * strcmp() below crashed the server before its first log line. Fall
+             * back to the runtime directory, which is what sStatDir defaults to. */
+            if (pValue == NULL)
+                pValue = DEFAULT_TMP_DIR;
         }
         verifyStatDir(pValue);
         m_sRTReportFile = sStatDir;
